From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:17:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Generate -webkit-text-fill-color for servo, not gecko only

Overlay code editors (a transparent textarea stacked on a highlighted
<pre>) hide the textarea's glyphs with -webkit-text-fill-color:
transparent and keep the caret visible with caret-color. Without the
property, the raw textarea text painted over the highlighted output.

The longhand is already fully defined here, but it was engine-gated to
gecko, so the servo build never got it. Dropping the gate generates it
into InheritedText for servo too, with initial value currentcolor, so
it stays inert until authored. blitz-paint reads it in the accompanying
patch.
---
 properties/longhands.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/properties/longhands.toml b/properties/longhands.toml
index ec939cc..a15afc7 100644
--- a/properties/longhands.toml
+++ b/properties/longhands.toml
@@ -2479,7 +2479,6 @@ affects = "layout"
 type = "Color"
 initial = "computed_value::T::currentcolor()"
 struct = "inherited_text"
-engine = "gecko"
 ignored_when_colors_disabled = true
 spec = "https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#the-webkit-text-fill-color"
 affects = "paint"
